.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "callsites [![Build Status](https://travis-ci.org/sindresorhus/callsites.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/sindresorhus/callsites)"
.PP
.RS 4
Get callsites from the \fRV8 stack trace API\fP 
.RE
.PP
.SH "Install"
.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install callsites
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
const callsites = require('callsites');

function unicorn() {
    console\&.log(callsites()[0]\&.getFileName());
    //=> '/Users/sindresorhus/dev/callsites/test\&.js'
}

unicorn();
.fi
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
Returns an array of callsite objects with the following methods:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRgetThis\fP: returns the value of \fRthis\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRgetTypeName\fP: returns the type of \fRthis\fP as a string\&. This is the name of the function stored in the constructor field of \fRthis\fP, if available, otherwise the object's \fR[[Class]]\fP internal property\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRgetFunction\fP: returns the current function\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRgetFunctionName\fP: returns the name of the current function, typically its \fRname\fP property\&. If a name property is not available an attempt will be made to try to infer a name from the function's context\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRgetMethodName\fP: returns the name of the property of \fRthis\fP or one of its prototypes that holds the current function\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRgetFileName\fP: if this function was defined in a script returns the name of the script\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRgetLineNumber\fP: if this function was defined in a script returns the current line number\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRgetColumnNumber\fP: if this function was defined in a script returns the current column number
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRgetEvalOrigin\fP: if this function was created using a call to \fReval\fP returns a string representing the location where \fReval\fP was called\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRisToplevel\fP: is this a top-level invocation, that is, is this the global object?
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRisEval\fP: does this call take place in code defined by a call to \fReval\fP?
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRisNative\fP: is this call in native V8 code?
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRisConstructor\fP: is this a constructor call?
.PP
